    {
      "question": "e-12763",
      "field": null,
      "attribute": "question/worked-solution",
      "old_sha256": "cb5d04750c00a409a3a7ad8e82a21e8cb0c6263f951062c409583a485ba71e5f",
      "new_sha256": "431e855ed5f9ae8db5047e6108b52fcedde65c1c7dbbc6ec7e931b1f3db9f3a4",
      "category": "ma_capture",
      "authoring": [],
      "source": [
        {
          "question": "e-12763",
          "field": null,
          "attribute": "question/worked-solution",
          "value": "The union of a family of indexed sets is the set containing all elements belonging to *at least one* set in the indexed family:\n\n$$\n\\bigcup_{i \\in I} A_i = \\big\\{ x\\in U \\: : \\: x \\in A_i \\:\\:\\textrm{for at least one } A_i,\\:\\: i \\in I \\big\\}\n$$\n\nwhere $U$ is a universal set.\n\nTherefore, in our case, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\u22c3}_{i\\in I}{S}_{i} & ={S}_{-1}\\cup {S}_{0}\\cup {S}_{1} \\\\  & =(-2,0)\\,\\cup \\,(-1,1)\\,\\cup \\,(0,2) \\\\  & =(-2,2).\\end{aligned}\n$$",
          "category": "ma_capture",
          "file": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038863/example-12763.json",
          "file_sha256": "62092102364635426c4b4d071229d0bdfe10c6585943fb6d6896f448c2c06cbc"
        }
